      ⍝ )EDIT reopens one after its last line; )? shows it, and )n
      ⍝ replaces line n at once, renumbering the lines.
      )EDIT RUN
[5]   )?
[0]   RUN N
[1]   ' *'[1+G]
[2]   G←GEN G
[3]   N←N-1
[4]   →(N>0)/1
[5]   )3
[3]   N←N-2
[5]   )?
[0]   RUN N
[1]   ' *'[1+G]
[2]   G←GEN G
[3]   N←N-2
[4]   →(N>0)/1
[5]   
      )FNS
GEN ROWS RUN SUM
      ⍝ )TRON names each line before it runs.
      )DEF Z←SQ X
[1]   Z←X×X
[2]   
      )TRON
      SQ 4
SQ[1]
16
      )TROFF
